          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "The ECB is actively pursuing stablecoin bans, MiCA reform acceleration, and a push to shift crypto firm oversight to ESMA, creating a dense and evolving compliance environment for any euro-adjacent crypto product.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "The ECB's own research documents that top 100 holders control over 80% of governance tokens in major DeFi protocols, and the digital euro by design centralizes euro-denominated digital payments under ECB infrastructure.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "ECB officials explicitly warned that US dollar-backed stablecoins risk draining EU capital, eroding Eurozone bank client bases and fees, and strengthening US monetary dominance at Europe's expense.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Euro stablecoins hold just 0.3% of total stablecoin supply, signaling thin eurozone liquidity in on-chain markets and structural dependence on dollar-denominated alternatives that the ECB is trying to counter.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart contract / DLT infrastructure",
          "level": "Low",
          "note": "The ECB's Pontes and Appia DLT pilots target controlled institutional settlement environments with central bank money, limiting smart contract exploit surface compared to permissionless DeFi deployments.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Macro / policy trap",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Oil shock-driven bond market volatility pushed French 10-year yields to 2011 highs and placed the ECB in a tighter policy trap than the Fed, constraining the ECB's room to support digital euro rollout while managing inflation and political instability.",
          "source": ""
        }
      ],
